license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. For every n >= 47 every integer from ceil((2n-8)/3) to n-2 is the size of a three-uniform Berge-C5-saturated hypergraph on n vertices, with unrestricted additions, so sat3(n, Berge-C5) <= ceil((2n-8)/3); the previous explicit bound had leading coefficient 4/3. The preprint classifies saturated cones, whose sizes start at ceil(6(n-1)/7), characterises saturated expansions of bipartite graphs with a degree-two side and gives exact values for n <= 11 from checked certificates; no general lower bound is proved. A Lean proof of the realized interval from ceil(2(n-1)/3) to n-2 for n >= 14 and of the values for n <= 7 is included. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
keywords:
